{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258953,"nonce":"6V3aMXHPEn9nWSLKcaabJjVFJZQ=","title":"os.exit and an uncaught error call libc exit while an LLVM promotion is in flight: SIGSEGV in beadie-promoter","message":"zylua's `os.exit` (`zl_os_exit` -\u003e `zb_exit`, bound to libc `exit`) and the uncaught-error path (`zb_exit(1)`) end the process with `exit`, which runs LLVM's C++ static destructors while the `beadie-promoter-1` thread may still be inside `MCJIT::emitObject` (`TargetPassConfig::addMachinePasses`, `PassRegistry::enumerateWith`). The promoter then faults: exit status 139 (sometimes 134) after the program's output is complete. The normal end of `run` does not hit it because main.rs `_exit`s.\n\nReproducer (Mac arm64, release llvm-backend build, ZYLUA_LLVM=1):\n\n    local function spin(n) local s = 0 for i = 1, n do s = s + (i * i) % 13 end return s end\n    for i = 1, 20000 do io.write(i, \" \", i * i, \"\\n\") end\n    print(spin(3000000))\n    os.exit(3)\n\nand the same with `error(\"boom\")` at the end in place of `os.exit(3)`. Seen on main dea6d08b (e.g. 15/30 runs of the error variant, 2/50 of the os.exit one) and on the s5 start-up branch (1/30, 11/50); the rate follows the promotion timing. Crash reports: faulting thread beadie-promoter-1 in LLVM codegen, the thread that called exit in `__cxa_finalize`.\n\nFix direction: route `zb_exit` through the same stop-then-`_exit` path the binaries use at the end of `run` (flushing Rust's stdout first), or stop the promoter before calling `exit`. Python's `sys.exit` uses the same builtin and should be checked too.","files":null}]}